From: Lilith Runtime Integration
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve shared session tool resources across auxiliary close

Background review, manual compression, and session-hygiene agents intentionally
alias a live session_id. Their close() must not tear down processes, terminal or
browser sessions, or computer-use target state owned by the primary agent.

Add explicit session tool-resource ownership, opt all three auxiliary paths out,
and cover lifecycle assignment, local cleanup, and captured-target preservation.

